      <description align="center" color="transparent" colored="true" height="103" resized="false" width="180" x="943" y="379">Perform moving average&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;O/P 1: actual data&lt;br&gt;O/P 2: model_alert&lt;br&gt;O/P 3: Model_Status&lt;br&gt;</description>
      <description align="center" color="purple" colored="true" height="654" resized="true" width="375" x="16" y="11">Data transformation &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Auther:&lt;br&gt;1. Akshay Hasabe&lt;br&gt;2. Naveen Kumar&lt;br&gt;3. Karthik sangapalli&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Overview:&lt;br&gt;This block do a bad data fliter by filtering those time stamps where model ccp logic is skip, then smooths data using a moving average while preserving critical tags for the optimizer. It skips smoothing if the model isn't live and filters out bad data, retaining only valid rows with timestamps &amp;#8805; end time for further processing.&lt;br&gt;Input:&lt;br&gt;1: Current data&lt;br&gt;2: model_alert&lt;br&gt;3: Model_Status&lt;br&gt;4: Flag_ma tags&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Output:&lt;br&gt;1: actual data&lt;br&gt;2: model_alert&lt;br&gt;3: Model_Status&lt;br&gt;</description>
